# REST Client (VS Code): execute sequencialmente, de cima para baixo.
# Use admin/manager para este roteiro (aprovação externa exige evidência).
# Informe IDs coerentes: veículo e orçamento pertencem ao mesmo cliente;
# o responsável deve ter papel technical, admin ou manager.
# expected_version é encadeado das respostas; não repita comandos já concluídos.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@cpf = 00000004774
@password = zjgb3A86OvCuj2Q6UcVPy9Ql
@token = {{workflowLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
@clientId = 3
@technicalId = 2
@budgetId = 53
@vehicleId = 1
@orderId = {{workflowCreate.response.body.$.order_id}}

### 1. Login — 200
# @name workflowLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"cpf": "{{cpf}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### 2. Criar OS — 201, recebida, version=1 (não enviar order_status)
# @name workflowCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": {{clientId}},
  "client_email": "cliente@example.com",
  "technical_id": {{technicalId}},
  "technical_name": "Técnico",
  "technical_email": "tecnico@example.com",
  "technical_responser_id": {{technicalId}},
  "technical_responser_name": "Responsável técnico",
  "technical_responser_email": "tecnico@example.com",
  "budget_id": {{budgetId}},
  "vehicle_id": {{vehicleId}},
  "service_name": "Troca de óleo e filtro",
  "service_description": "Inspeção e manutenção",
  "duration_service_hours": 24
}

### 3. Ações disponíveis — 200, [start_diagnosis]
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/allowed-actions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Salto proibido — 409, sem alterar a versão
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expected_version": {{workflowCreate.response.body.$.version}}, "received_by": "Cliente"}

### 5. Iniciar diagnóstico — 200, em_diagnostico
# @name workflowDiagnosis
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/start-diagnosis
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expected_version": {{workflowCreate.response.body.$.version}}}

### 6. Solicitar aprovação — 200, aguardando_aprovacao; congela o orçamento
# @name workflowRequestApproval
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/request-approval
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expected_version": {{workflowDiagnosis.response.body.$.version}},
  "diagnosis": "Óleo vencido e filtro saturado; substituir ambos."
}

### 7. Execução sem aprovação — 409 approval_required
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/start-execution
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expected_version": {{workflowRequestApproval.response.body.$.version}}}

### 8. Registrar aprovação externa — 200, permanece aguardando_aprovacao
# Um cliente autenticado pode aprovar a própria OS sem evidence.
# @name workflowApprove
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expected_version": {{workflowRequestApproval.response.body.$.version}},
  "evidence": "Autorização do cliente registrada no atendimento presencial, protocolo 123."
}

### 9. Iniciar execução — 200, em_execucao, execution_started_at preenchido
# @name workflowExecution
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/start-execution
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expected_version": {{workflowApprove.response.body.$.version}}}

### 10. Finalizar — 200, finalizada, finished_at preenchido
# @name workflowFinish
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/finish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expected_version": {{workflowExecution.response.body.$.version}},
  "service_report": "Óleo e filtro substituídos; testes de funcionamento concluídos."
}

### 11. Entregar — 200, entregue, delivered_at preenchido
# @name workflowDeliver
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expected_version": {{workflowFinish.response.body.$.version}},
  "received_by": "Cliente responsável pelo veículo"
}

### 12. Estado terminal — 200, allowed_actions=[]
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/allowed-actions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Histórico — 200, seis eventos em ordem de versão
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/history?offset=0&limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Histórico paginado — 200, dois eventos
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/history?offset=1&limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Repetição com versão antiga — 409 stale_order_version
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expected_version": {{workflowFinish.response.body.$.version}}, "received_by": "Cliente"}

### 16. Tentativa de contornar o fluxo — 422
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"order_status": "recebida"}

### 17. OS entregue preservada para auditoria — 409 order_deletion_disabled
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
